<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardino Rivadavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1780–1845</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernardino Rivadavia was an Argentine statesman and the first President of the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>, in 1826–1827. As a minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> province in the early 1820s he founded the University of Buenos Aires, reformed the Church and public finances and encouraged immigration. His centralist constitution of 1826 and the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> provoked the provinces, and he resigned in 1827 and died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernardino-rivadavia.jpg" alt="Bernardino Rivadavia" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernardino_Rivadavia_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
